From fbbed960b2f0c3162440ac2ce16d13ad64292903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mechres <164776284+Mechres@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:06:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: sun6i: exper-t8e: Keep the SDIO Wi-Fi powered in
 suspend

Without keep-power-in-suspend the mmc host does not advertise
MMC_PM_KEEP_POWER, so brcmfmac fails with "Failed to set pm_flags 1" on
suspend and "HT Avail request error: -110" on resume, and the chip is
unusable afterwards.

Verified on the tablet with a 30 s s2idle (rtcwake): no brcmfmac errors,
scan works after resume. Wake-up by the Wi-Fi host-wake line was not
tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts
index 021574646..51b4d5e23 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts
@@ -110,6 +110,7 @@ &mmc1 {
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&wifi_pwrseq>;
 	bus-width = <4>;
 	non-removable;
+	keep-power-in-suspend;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	brcmf: wifi@1 {
-- 
